00:03:26.590 --> 00:03:31.000
So what are the key challenges
that these type of customers

00:03:31.000 --> 00:03:35.940
face when they have workstation
high-performance workloads?

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:38.410
So number one that
we see the most often

00:03:38.410 --> 00:03:41.470
is that they need to
protect their valuable IP.

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:46.180
So imagine a media
entertainment studio

00:03:46.180 --> 00:03:52.600
creating next "Avengers" didn't
want a spoiler to leak out,

00:03:52.600 --> 00:03:55.510
and the federal government
didn't want any classified data

00:03:55.510 --> 00:03:56.180
to leak out.

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:59.260
So it really is number one
for all of those use cases

00:03:59.260 --> 00:04:00.980
I described.

00:04:00.980 --> 00:04:03.100
Another one is
on-site hardware is

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:05.210
expensive to scale and manage.

00:04:05.210 --> 00:04:07.400
So if you are
purchasing workstations,

00:04:07.400 --> 00:04:09.310
they are under the desk.

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:13.750
If you need to scale,
grow, hire more people--

00:04:13.750 --> 00:04:17.890
contractors-- or vendors need
to get access and work with you,

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:21.550
it's more complicated
to have to wait six

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:22.930
weeks to get the workstation.

00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:25.480
And you may not need
it all year long.

00:04:25.480 --> 00:04:28.920
Did you get your ROI on it?

00:04:28.920 --> 00:04:30.920
That's a common problem as well.

00:04:30.920 --> 00:04:33.100
And then, modern and
mobile workforces

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:35.110
are demanding offset access.

00:04:35.110 --> 00:04:38.900
So this is people collaborating.

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:42.250
This is people wanting
to work from home.

00:04:42.250 --> 00:04:46.630
It's more and more common,
have that work-life balance.

00:04:46.630 --> 00:04:49.810
And with workstations,
the 3D models,

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:52.180
the graphics-intensive
workloads, the content

00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:56.240
itself is increasing in
size as well as complexity.

00:04:56.240 --> 00:05:00.130
So when teams and different
vendors or contractors

00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:02.230
have to collaborate
together, it's

00:05:02.230 --> 00:05:04.540
more and more difficult
because the content

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:07.660
itself is more complex.

00:05:07.660 --> 00:05:12.220
And there's the need to have
geographically-dispersed teams.

00:05:12.220 --> 00:05:15.250
You might want to hire people
from different locations

00:05:15.250 --> 00:05:18.370
in the world because
of cost savings,

00:05:18.370 --> 00:05:22.510
because a company may have
purchased another company, lots

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:25.470
of reasons.

00:05:25.470 --> 00:05:28.180
OK.

00:05:28.180 --> 00:05:29.560
Those are the challenges.

00:05:29.560 --> 00:05:34.450
And here, I covered how
virtual workstations

00:05:34.450 --> 00:05:36.127
can address those challenges.

00:05:36.127 --> 00:05:37.210
These are not all of them.

00:05:37.210 --> 00:05:39.585
There's a lot more to it, but
these are a few highlighted

00:05:39.585 --> 00:05:40.300
ones.

00:05:40.300 --> 00:05:44.823
And this is together with
public cloud like Google

00:05:44.823 --> 00:05:46.990
as well as our PCoIP
technology and all the benefits

00:05:46.990 --> 00:05:47.810
you get out of it.

00:05:47.810 --> 00:05:52.610
One is that it improves
productivity and efficiency.

00:05:52.610 --> 00:05:55.780
So now that your workstation
is no longer under your desk,

00:05:55.780 --> 00:05:58.750
it's somewhere else
consolidated in a public cloud

00:05:58.750 --> 00:06:02.503
or in a data center, you get
to access it from anywhere.

00:06:02.503 --> 00:06:04.420
That means you can have
those dispersed teams.

00:06:04.420 --> 00:06:07.930
You don't need to worry
about different team

00:06:07.930 --> 00:06:10.330
members downloading data
to their workstation

00:06:10.330 --> 00:06:14.110
to work on it then uploading
so the other person can

00:06:14.110 --> 00:06:15.790
see what changed.

00:06:15.790 --> 00:06:18.760
It's just more
efficient this way.

00:06:18.760 --> 00:06:21.250
And working from
home, there's been

00:06:21.250 --> 00:06:24.310
lots of case studies
done around that,

00:06:24.310 --> 00:06:30.250
how it improves efficiency in
collaboration by 25% or more.

00:06:30.250 --> 00:06:33.800
So it's generally a more
efficient way to work.

00:06:33.800 --> 00:06:39.190
And lastly, it does enable
companies to hire global talent

00:06:39.190 --> 00:06:40.060
from anywhere.

00:06:40.060 --> 00:06:43.600
So they don't have to
feel the labor pinch

00:06:43.600 --> 00:06:46.172
having to locally hire in
whatever office they're in,

00:06:46.172 --> 00:06:47.380
in whatever city they are in.

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:51.280
They can hire anywhere and
benefit even from taxes--

00:06:51.280 --> 00:06:55.400
tax deductions, as well.

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:58.900
Another one is that you can
realize unprecedented security

00:06:58.900 --> 00:07:00.190
and protect your IP.

00:07:00.190 --> 00:07:02.567
So with our technology, when
you remote your workstation

00:07:02.567 --> 00:07:04.150
somewhere else,
firstly, again, you're

00:07:04.150 --> 00:07:05.210
not downloading the data.

00:07:05.210 --> 00:07:06.585
So it's not
somewhere on a device

00:07:06.585 --> 00:07:08.830
that somebody is taking,
traveling with, working

00:07:08.830 --> 00:07:10.390
from home with.

00:07:10.390 --> 00:07:15.150
The data is somewhere safe in
the cloud or the data center.

00:07:15.150 --> 00:07:19.170
And with our technology, what
we do is we look at that desktop

00:07:19.170 --> 00:07:22.080
that you are working within--

00:07:22.080 --> 00:07:26.830
like an application, Autodesk
Maya, AutoCAD, or something

00:07:26.830 --> 00:07:28.520
like that.

00:07:28.520 --> 00:07:30.730
We just encrypt and
encode the desktop,

00:07:30.730 --> 00:07:34.990
and we transmit only encrypted
pixels to the client device,

00:07:34.990 --> 00:07:36.010
not the actual data.

00:07:36.010 --> 00:07:37.510
So the data is
protected in a cloud.

00:07:37.510 --> 00:07:39.850
It never gets sent
to the client device,

00:07:39.850 --> 00:07:41.320
and that's really important.

00:07:41.320 --> 00:07:43.090
And second, if you're
using Google Cloud--

00:07:43.090 --> 00:07:45.640
I mean, as you have seen
at the keynote and a lot

00:07:45.640 --> 00:07:49.000
of the sessions here,
they've put a lot of effort

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:53.740
into security, like
compliances, certifications,

00:07:53.740 --> 00:07:56.320
encryption of your
data, lot of products

00:07:56.320 --> 00:07:57.705
that they offer around security.

00:07:57.705 --> 00:07:59.830
So the combination of the
two makes it more secure.

00:08:02.900 --> 00:08:05.890
By virtualizing, it also
increases your agility

00:08:05.890 --> 00:08:07.760
and scalability.

00:08:07.760 --> 00:08:13.240
So you can get on-demand access
to latest tech all the time--

00:08:13.240 --> 00:08:16.460
and as much of it as you want.

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:19.630
So for example, NVIDIA
launched a new GPU, T4,

00:08:19.630 --> 00:08:22.630
and you get to utilize it
immediately rather than

00:08:22.630 --> 00:08:27.750
wait for you to order it, to
arrive, to get it and use it.

00:08:27.750 --> 00:08:33.190
And hopefully, when you
purchase something on-premises,

00:08:33.190 --> 00:08:35.012
you hopefully we
use it all the time.

00:08:35.012 --> 00:08:36.429
Otherwise, you
don't get your ROI.

00:08:36.429 --> 00:08:40.397
With public cloud, you get the
scale, use it-- a lot of it.

00:08:40.397 --> 00:08:41.980
And then, if you
don't use it anymore,

00:08:41.980 --> 00:08:43.740
you don't pay for it anymore.

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:49.100
It's that OpEx versus CapEx
model and the benefits of that.

00:08:49.100 --> 00:08:53.540
And lastly, by virtualizing
your workstation,

00:08:53.540 --> 00:08:56.710
you really realize the full
potential of the cloud.

00:08:56.710 --> 00:08:59.530
So you are moving your
data to the cloud,

00:08:59.530 --> 00:09:02.660
consolidating your data
with your compute--

00:09:02.660 --> 00:09:05.830
so all the compute
power for rendering,

00:09:05.830 --> 00:09:09.038
high-performance computing--

00:09:09.038 --> 00:09:10.580
but you're not doing
the workstation.

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:12.670
So whatever your result
is of your render,

00:09:12.670 --> 00:09:14.170
now you have to
download it and work

00:09:14.170 --> 00:09:16.930
on it if it's an application.

00:09:16.930 --> 00:09:19.740
When you move, you co-locate
your data, your compute,

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:20.490
and your graphics.

00:09:20.490 --> 00:09:24.850
You move your workstation
where your data is.

00:09:24.850 --> 00:09:29.500
You get to benefit
fully from the cloud.

00:09:29.500 --> 00:09:34.230
And really, this is
only possible if,

00:09:34.230 --> 00:09:38.560
when you are virtualizing, that
you have that really great user

00:09:38.560 --> 00:09:39.160
experience.

00:09:39.160 --> 00:09:43.780
You can expect your
high-performance users

00:09:43.780 --> 00:09:46.960
to use their
workstations sluggish

00:09:46.960 --> 00:09:48.980
or less distortions on it.

00:09:48.980 --> 00:09:50.005
That's where we come in.

00:09:50.005 --> 00:09:53.410
We ensure that
their performance is

00:09:53.410 --> 00:09:55.900
as if it's under the desk
rather than somewhere else.

00:09:59.085 --> 00:10:00.450
OK.

00:10:00.450 --> 00:10:02.180
So why Teradici?

00:10:02.180 --> 00:10:03.868
Why our technology?

