virtualized and on-premises,

00:10:26.840 --> 00:10:33.290
it's 100% color accurate,
lossless, build-to-lossless,

00:10:33.290 --> 00:10:36.320
and highly interactive
and low latency,

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:39.950
which is what these type of
users really, really need.

00:10:39.950 --> 00:10:42.370
Also, what we do in terms
of high-performance user

00:10:42.370 --> 00:10:44.120
experience is that we
automatically adjust

00:10:44.120 --> 00:10:45.630
to changing network conditions.

00:10:45.630 --> 00:10:49.100
So if your users are working
from home or traveling wherever

00:10:49.100 --> 00:10:54.050
they are-- using a tablet
maybe somewhere in the field,

00:10:54.050 --> 00:10:59.510
example would be architect going
on site and looking at his 3D

00:10:59.510 --> 00:11:00.595
drawings on his tablet--

00:11:00.595 --> 00:11:02.470
well, the network is
very different from when

00:11:02.470 --> 00:11:03.230
he is in the office.

00:11:03.230 --> 00:11:05.813
We automatically adjust and give
you the best user experience.

00:11:05.813 --> 00:11:11.360
There's no need to do some
change settings, et cetera.

00:11:11.360 --> 00:11:14.060
We also offer ultra secure
remoting and endpoint

00:11:14.060 --> 00:11:15.260
architecture.

00:11:15.260 --> 00:11:19.300
Like I said, we just encrypt
and transmit pixels--

00:11:19.300 --> 00:11:21.500
AES-256 encryption as well.

00:11:21.500 --> 00:11:24.440
And no data ever gets
to the client device.

00:11:24.440 --> 00:11:26.780
Again, I'll emphasize here
that one of our verticals

00:11:26.780 --> 00:11:28.960
is the federal government--

00:11:28.960 --> 00:11:30.950
it's quite a big
vertical for us--

00:11:30.950 --> 00:11:35.970
