00:33:01.405 --> 00:33:03.280
One of the neat things
about the GCP machines

00:33:03.280 --> 00:33:05.810
is they start up really fast.

00:33:05.810 --> 00:33:09.020
So within less than a minute,
this machine will be running.

00:33:09.020 --> 00:33:12.220
And then, your user will
automatically connect to it.

00:33:12.220 --> 00:33:14.410
It's important to keep
control of your costs

00:33:14.410 --> 00:33:19.210
because running machines in the
cloud, especially the GPU ones,

00:33:19.210 --> 00:33:20.740
can run up a large bill.

00:33:20.740 --> 00:33:23.200
So some users like
to turn them off when

00:33:23.200 --> 00:33:24.250
